    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 14 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the registration-date default on `POST /api/owners`. When no `registrationDate` is supplied it now defaults to the server's current date, and owners return `registrationDate` in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format (a supplied date is preserved).\n\nChanges:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` field (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so it's accepted on create and returned on the `Owner` response (which `allOf`-includes `OwnerFields`). The OpenAPI generator maps `format: date` to `LocalDate`, and MapStruct wires it through automatically.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field (`@Column(name = \"registration_date\")`) with getter/setter.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when the incoming value is null.\n- **Schema files** (h2, hsqldb, postgres, mysql) \u2014 added a `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table.\n\nThe active persistence path is Spring Data JPA, so the entity mapping handles reads/writes; the JDBC row mappers didn't need changes. The `format: date` serialization produces the required ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` output.",
